= The Centre: advisers

The Centre is the party of its apparatus: Meyer who mediates, Zetkin who keeps the women and the unity, Pieck who counts the money, Eberlein who keeps the books for the Comintern. Each can act once every three months. A faction that is not consulted for six months while it still has real strength grows angry.

- @meyer
- @zetkin
- @pieck
- @eberlein
- @root: Return to main

@meyer
title: Ernst Meyer: mediate between the wings
subtitle: Bring Left and Right to one table. · dev: kf_right_dissent −3, kf_centre_dissent −3, kf_left_dissent −3, adv_centre_last = time
unavailable-subtitle: [? if meyer_timer > 0 : [+ meyer_timer +] months before Meyer can act again. ?]
choose-if: meyer_timer = 0
on-arrival: meyer_timer = 3; kf_right_dissent -= 3; kf_centre_dissent -= 3; kf_left_dissent -= 3; adv_centre_last = time

Meyer, who has carried the party through the quarrels since the March Action, finds a formula in which both wings can read their own case. It will not hold forever, and for this month it does.

@zetkin
title: Clara Zetkin: appeal for unity
subtitle: A letter from the old comrade. · dev: kf_right_dissent −2, kf_centre_dissent −2, kf_left_dissent −2, trust +2, adv_centre_last = time
unavailable-subtitle: [? if zetkin_timer > 0 : [+ zetkin_timer +] months before Zetkin can act again. ?]
choose-if: zetkin_timer = 0
on-arrival: zetkin_timer = 3; kf_right_dissent -= 2; kf_centre_dissent -= 2; kf_left_dissent -= 2; comintern_trust += 2; adv_centre_last = time

Zetkin, who knew Rosa, writes to the whole party. Few will contradict her, and the letter is read aloud in district meetings from Stuttgart to Königsberg.

@pieck
title: Wilhelm Pieck: put the finances in order
subtitle: Collect the arrears and the dues. · dev: resources +1, kf_centre_strength +1, adv_centre_last = time
unavailable-subtitle: [? if pieck_timer > 0 : [+ pieck_timer +] months before Pieck can act again. ?]
choose-if: pieck_timer = 0
on-arrival: pieck_timer = 3; resources += 1; kf_centre_strength += 1; adv_centre_last = time

Pieck goes through the books of the districts, one by one, and the arrears begin to come in. The party is a membership organisation, and it runs on dues.

@eberlein
title: Hugo Eberlein: account to the Comintern
subtitle: Report on money and cadres. · dev: trust +3, resources +1, adv_centre_last = time
unavailable-subtitle: [? if eberlein_timer > 0 : [+ eberlein_timer +] months before Eberlein can act again. ?]
choose-if: eberlein_timer = 0
on-arrival: eberlein_timer = 3; comintern_trust += 3; resources += 1; adv_centre_last = time

Eberlein, who has carried the party's secret funds and its contacts to Moscow, makes his report. The Comintern is never unwilling to check the accounts of a party it pays for.
